<title>NEW ZEALAND: Lion Pepsi sale not in the pipeline.</title>
<headline>Lion Pepsi sale not in the pipeline.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lion Nathan Ltd Chief Executive Douglas Myers said on Monday the brewer was not about to sell its interest in the Australian joint venture it has with PepsiCo Inc, contrary to market speculation.</p>
<p>Myers said in an interview that there was nothing in the rumour, which suggested Lion was about to sell its interest to Cadbury Schweppes Plc.</p>
<p>&quot;I've said a year or so ago that, long-term, it makes sense but there is nothing on the boil,&quot; Myers said.  </p>
<p>Lion has an 83.54 percent interest in the loss-making joint venture and Pepsico has 16.46 percent with an option to move to 25 percent.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
